Java keywords, reserved and literals:
- All are lowercase
- Cannot be used as Identifiers(user defined words)

For example:
- Control program flow: if, else, continue, break, for, do, while, switch, case, default.
- Describe Code Structure: private, public, import, package, class, static, final, return, void.
- Define types: byte, int, double, boolean, var.
- Literal values: true, false, null.
- Work with objects: new, this, super.
- Handle exception: try, catch.

Java identifiers
- Any custom name given to the variables, methods or class by the programmer are called identifiers.